,"signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b92843e4b0b8eefb83c9649a9266ef5b78146d39f6df2020e048f23583617729","event_uuid":"9047bdb1-92d7-416e-8b98-f686ce4edcdf","position":{"commit_sha":"856a03cecc981184ec7d046eb4e7868a2141f2a8","position":"1786249191290795001-9047bdb1-92d7-416e-8b98-f686ce4edcdf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Held-out validation after implementation attempt 1: restored the separate oracle and ran all four ticket test files. Result: 6 failed, 6 passed. Missing contracts: canonical preview plan omitted exact field drift; argparse accepted prefix abbreviations of the legacy dry-run option; and the real preview path passed route into an incompletely updated pass context. Re-dispatched to the held-out implementer with behavioral contracts only; withheld test source remains undisclosed.","timestamp":1786238654709354001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"ADR convention check: ADR 0092 keeps its unique four-digit filename/slug and matching docs/adr/.numbers/0092 marker. Updated the decision text to distinguish canonical retained manifests from legacy uncapped LIVE deletion, regenerated the derived ADR index, and verified scripts/check_adr_numbers.py plus gen_adr_index.py --check. The 19-test numbering/index suite passes.","timestamp":1786238988070932001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed Gerrit change 1554 (04933de298, Change-Id I7a820c313f94abe14743e0b217b5ebf9e027ac48) after fetching and fast-forwarding to origin/main b7d29e58c7; pre-push behind count was 0. TDD evidence: initial oracle RED 6/12, implementation cycles reached 12/12 held-out green; defect-seeded mutations independently broke route forwarding and lock bypass. Quality review added a RED exact-failure-tally regression before the fix. Post-base-update validation: 202 focused bridge/reconciler tests, 19 ADR numbering/index tests, make lint, make typecheck, ADR generators/checks. Full default suite was delegated to CI per operator instruction after its only early stale preview-lock expectations were corrected in targeted suites.","timestamp":1786240351204673001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit patch set 1 CI ran 11,553 default-suite tests green on Linux; its only failures were two complexity-baseline self-tests because the structural refactor lowered main() from ceiling 23 to 20. Applied the sanctioned shrink-only baseline update (no ceiling increase), verified 72 baseline tests plus make lint, amended as 2fc86797e3, fetched origin/main again with behind count 0, and pushed patch set 2. LLM-Review +1 was correctly invalidated and will re-run.","timestamp":1786241242859250001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Addressed all four patch-set-1 LLM advisories in patch set 3 (70319740c7). Major compatibility finding fixed in scope: canonical rendering now applies only to preview/sync, so route=legacy bootstrap retains outbound/inbound manifest shape; regression was RED first. Exact canonical tally now uses actually dispatched inbound plus post-suppression outbound candidates; suppressed-inbound regression was RED first. Added capped canonical sync coverage (plan/counts/max_changes/deferred) and missing/corrupt batch-manifest fallback coverage. Validation: 30 focused compatibility tests, 279 bridge/orchestrator+complexity tests, lint, typecheck. Fetched origin/main immediately before push; behind count 0.","timestamp":1786241620124758001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"ADR convention verification: ADR 0092 retains its unique canonical filename and matching docs/adr/.numbers/0092 marker, whose content names that filename; docs/adr/README.md remains generated and current. Patch-set-3 CI has passed both the ADR-number bijection gate and ADR-index drift gate. Worktree was fetched from origin and remains 0 commits behind origin/main.","timestamp":1786241962618813001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patch-set-3 CI diagnosis: Ubuntu/Python 3.11 ran 11,560 tests green but an xdist worker crashed while executing unrelated tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py::test_matching_guard_is_accepted; coverage then fell to 14.66% because the worker crash truncated execution. The change does not touch opcert code or that test. Treating this as infrastructure/test-worker flake; no code change is justified. Will request Gerrit recheck after the remaining macOS job concludes.","timestamp":1786242787716497001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Recheck run 31290743251: Ubuntu/Python 3.12 produced a different unrelated single-test failure after 11,559 passes: tests/interfaces/store/test_git_contention_9305.py::test_concurrent_processes_through_seam_both_succeed had one subprocess return 1. This test and store/gitutil are outside the patch; the same lane passed on run 31289893832. Classified as a pre-existing contention flake, not bridge behavior. Waiting for remaining lanes before another recheck.","timestamp":1786243927180899001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Recurring flake disposition: linked existing opcert worker-crash bug 2207-2917-e21b-42bd as discovered_from this story. Filed and linked new bug ac76-0416-7f61-4a2b for the independently flaky concurrent Git-writer seam, with run 31290743251 evidence and deterministic regression acceptance criteria. Neither flake is being smuggled into this bridge change.","timestamp":1786244527707120001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 1554 patch set 3 passed LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with zero unresolved comments on CI run 31293144328, then merged at 2026-08-09T04:15:40Z. The GitHub mirror now contains merged commit 43e822a83fc866f184073fbf08edcb6dd649dbf2. The bridge worktree was fetched from origin and rebased onto origin/main; Git skipped the already-applied local patch and HEAD now equals the mirrored merge with behind count 0.","timestamp":1786249191290795001}],"created_at":1786047582784571001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f79e39e5-1f30-4312-b33f-b3fb6bf0522d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4752-3afb-e8bd-448a"},{"link_uuid":"6429d54d-e337-4739-bd9c-5b31c292e0b4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1ecd-ab6e-c36e-43be"},{"link_uuid":"ca0723bd-9059-4717-a7a9-d74445ec1b2d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1402-7370-5c86-458e"},{"link_uuid":"d8c8c295-4024-4a63-a2a1-ba1344c347d3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"083a-f596-a7c2-4e27"}],"description":"## Context\n\n`rebar bridge preview` is now the canonical dry-run command. It does NOT replace legacy `--mode reconcile-check`: reconcile-check remains a distinct lock-free diagnostic that scans cached bound pairs, performs unarbitrated comparison, and writes `bridge_state/reconcile-check.json`. Older workflows and environments must keep that behavior unchanged.\n\nThis story improves only the canonical preview/sync presentation and removes the dangerous argparse abbreviation path. Preview already runs the ordinary dry-run differ, whose plan entries contain the arbitrated field-level `changed` detail. It should render the plan and that drift detail from the SAME pass instead of launching or reimplementing reconcile-check.\n\nCanonical preview must also be lock-free. Today the dry-run route enters the pass-lock ceremony and can call `_purge_committed_reconciler_locks`, even though it never applies mutations. The canonical route will load a coherent read-only snapshot and produce its manifest without acquiring, purging, stealing, or writing the pass lock. Legacy reconcile-check remains independently lock-free through its existing diagnostic branch.\n\n## Compatibility boundary\n\nThe migration remains expand-contract:\n\n- `rebar reconcile --mode reconcile-check` keeps its all-cached-ticket loader, unarbitrated `_compare_pair` behavior, diagnostic JSON artifact, output, and exit semantics. `_compare_pair` is retained because its contract is intentionally not derivable from the arbitrated dry-run differ.\n- Legacy `rebar reconcile --mode dry-run` and direct-engine `--mode dry-run` retain their existing observable behavior.\n- Legacy `rebar reconcile --mode live`, library `rebar.reconcile(mode=\"live\")`, MCP `reconcile(mode=\"live\")`, older workflow revisions, and external helpers retain the historical uncapped-LIVE tally/no-retained-manifest contract.\n- Canonical `bridge preview` and `bridge sync` gain the comparable manifest contract. A route-level normalized-request field selects that presentation; it must not infer canonical behavior from `Mode.LIVE` or rewrite the Mode ladder.\n- Undocumented argparse prefix abbreviations are not compatibility vocabulary. The documented-but-invalid `rebar reconcile --dry-run` typo currently abbreviates `--dry-run-enumerate`, prints ticket directories, and exits 0. `allow_abbrev=False` makes such unknown/abbreviated options fail with invocation error 2 before reads, locks, or mutation; documented `--mode dry-run` remains valid.\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n1. Extend the normalized request with an explicit canonical-manifest/route disposition and thread it through `run_pass`, `reconcile_once`, and the existing renderer seam. Keep legacy callers defaulted to the old presentation.\n2. For canonical preview, use the ordinary active-ticket dry-run path once, carry each differ plan entry plus its existing `changed` field detail into a combined manifest, and bypass pass-lock acquisition/purge/release. Do not invoke reconcile-check and do not duplicate `_compare_pair`.\n3. Make canonical sync retain the same field-comparable manifest envelope as preview, including uncapped canonical live. Record applied/failed tally in that manifest. Keep legacy uncapped LIVE deletion/tally behavior unchanged; capped canonical sync and bootstrap compatibility modes retain their existing deterministic applied/deferred contracts.\n4. Set `allow_abbrev=False` on the engine parser. Correct current docs to use `bridge preview` or explicit legacy `--mode dry-run`; document that reconcile-check remains distinct and that legacy live output is unchanged.\n\n## Test plan\n\nRED-first held-out tests exercise real CLI/direct-engine entrypoints and persisted state:\n\n- Canonical preview produces one manifest containing both arbitrated plan entries and exact field-level drift from the same differ pass; the fixture proves active-ticket loading occurs once.\n- A held pass lock and a purge spy prove canonical preview neither acquires nor mutates pass-lock refs. Unrelated ticket, binding, snapshot, diagnostic, and lock state remains byte-identical.\n- Legacy reconcile-check still scans its broader cached-ticket set, retains `_compare_pair`, writes the same `bridge_state/reconcile-check.json`, and remains lock-free.\n- Canonical preview and canonical sync over the same store expose the same field-comparable manifest keys. Canonical live retains its manifest and exact applied/failed tally.\n- Legacy `--mode live`, library reconcile, MCP reconcile, older workflow command shapes, and the external compatibility helper retain the old tally/no-retained-manifest surface.\n- `--dry-run` and another abbreviated/unknown option exit 2 before any repository or lock mutation; `--mode dry-run` still succeeds.\n\nMutation checks remove the canonical route disposition and the preview lock bypass in turn; the held-out canonical-manifest and no-lock tests must go RED. No contention harness is added because preview removes a lock rather than composing writes, while sync continues through the existing single pass lock.\n\nSurface parity census:\n\n- CLI: in scope for canonical preview/sync and legacy reconcile compatibility.\n- Direct engine: in scope for canonical subcommands and legacy `--mode`.\n- Library: continuity-only; `rebar.reconcile(...)` remains on the legacy presentation until the bridge library story.\n- MCP: continuity-only; MCP `reconcile` remains on the legacy presentation until the bridge MCP story.\n- Automated callers: current workflow canonical commands gain the new manifest; older workflow revisions and external compatibility helpers remain valid.\n- Dual direction: preview and canonical sync share a comparable manifest, while preview remains non-mutating and sync applies.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Canonical `bridge preview` runs one ordinary dry-run differ pass and emits one manifest containing the arbitrated plan plus exact field-level drift from that same pass.\n- [ ] Canonical preview acquires, purges, steals, and writes no pass lock, and collateral repository/ref state remains unchanged.\n- [ ] Legacy `--mode reconcile-check` retains its all-cached-ticket loader, `_compare_pair` semantics, lock-free execution, diagnostic JSON artifact, output, and exit behavior.\n- [ ] Canonical preview reads the active local-ticket set once; it does not launch reconcile-check or duplicate a second comparison pass.\n- [ ] The parser uses `allow_abbrev=False`; abbreviated or unknown options exit 2 before reads, locks, or mutation, while documented legacy options remain valid.\n- [ ] Canonical preview and canonical sync emit the same field-comparable manifest envelope; canonical uncapped live retains a manifest with the exact applied/failed tally.\n- [ ] Legacy uncapped LIVE callers through CLI, direct engine, library, MCP, older workflows, and external helpers retain the historical tally/no-retained-manifest contract.\n- [ ] Existing capped canonical sync and legacy bootstrap applied/deferred partitions remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Current docs use `bridge preview` for dry-run guidance and explicitly document reconcile-check and legacy live-output continuity.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py`: explicit canonical-vs-legacy presentation disposition; `allow_abbrev=False`.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`: route-level lock bypass for canonical preview while preserving reconcile-check.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py`: carry canonical presentation and same-pass drift through the pass.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_planning.py`: canonical live retained-manifest branch without changing legacy LIVE.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/manifest_renderer.py`: one canonical preview/sync envelope renderer.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_check.py`: compatibility control only; `_compare_pair` and artifact remain.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/`: parser, lock, one-pass, manifest, and legacy compatibility oracles.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/`: real CLI/library/MCP parity and abbreviation regression.\n- `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/cli-reference.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`: canonical guidance plus retained legacy contracts.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py","reason":"disable argparse abbreviation and reuse the existing route discriminator"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py","reason":"bypass pass-lock ceremony only for canonical preview and forward its route"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py","reason":"carry route and same-pass canonical manifest through the pass"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py","reason":"render exact field details in canonical plan entries without changing legacy entries"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py","reason":"thread the canonical route to existing planning and rendering seams"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_planning.py","reason":"retain canonical uncapped-live manifest while preserving legacy LIVE tally and deletion"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/manifest_renderer.py","reason":"reuse existing field helpers for one comparable canonical preview/sync envelope"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_check.py","reason":"compatibility control; retain distinct comparison and diagnostic artifact"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_bridge_canonical_manifest.py","reason":"RED-first happy path for lock-free preview and canonical retained manifest"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_bridge_preview_one_pass_heldout.py","reason":"held-out same-pass drift, parser edge, and legacy engine continuity oracles"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_manifest_compat_heldout.py","reason":"held-out real parser and library/MCP compatibility oracles"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_preview_under_sync_contention_heldout.py","reason":"held-out complete-or-loud read integrity under pass and tracker contention"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py","reason":"pin legacy MCP reconcile presentation"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_library.py","reason":"pin legacy library reconcile presentation"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"canonical dry-run guidance and reconcile-check distinction"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"generated command and output contract"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"migration and compatibility notes"},{"path":"docs/adr/0092-bridge-primary-vocabulary-compatibility-adapters.md","reason":"align the accepted decision with canonical retained manifests while preserving legacy LIVE"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","4752-3afb-e8bd-448a"],["parent","2f79-2b32-28c5-4eb3"],["relates_to","083a-f596-a7c2-4e27"],["relates_to","1402-7370-5c86-458e"],["relates_to","1ecd-ab6e-c36e-43be"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f79-2b32-28c5-4eb3","parent_status_uuid":"7efea083-a6bc-4330-9502-422a7a52a31f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["bridge"],"ticket_id":"424f-bc35-b7ca-419a","ticket_type":"story","title":"Merge preview into one pass and make the abbreviation bug impossible","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3f180b25-8551-4cac-8e26-4333b777f242","59697f7b-abd5-433f-bea5-1b6c3fefe6e6","61960a46-9f6f-410a-a7a9-b91c99de9045","f79e39e5-1f30-4312-b33f-b3fb6bf0522d","3d93c65b-fc37-40bc-9cf6-5f7b19023d26","b0d936f1-920c-49be-9933-d6874f65074f","470d487e-bc4d-443a-973c-dbd3c9b19d2e","7efea083-a6bc-4330-9502-422a7a52a31f","30e015b3-43b0-4d59-bcf5-d9548aabf69a","ee134228-4a42-453b-af3e-940fb899774d","e3bd2d7e-e408-4a0f-b5c4-2f4f251e198b","c0a13c09-31e3-45f8-b461-bbd52902b09c","5916bdd8-2dba-496c-bc19-753b16a22a46","6429d54d-e337-4739-bd9c-5b31c292e0b4","884291d1-64ef-406a-a75e-e111b1c6c24b","989c886c-3014-4352-baa7-741c4665c864","ca0723bd-9059-4717-a7a9-d74445ec1b2d","4403c230-4683-4e92-a5cc-70defec5c326","d8c8c295-4024-4a63-a2a1-ba1344c347d3","2a86ee87-0949-4716-87e2-46e62fc790f4","5375e65d-b87b-4d63-b0d2-cf08c8c3200c","bb34d451-5496-49a6-bb83-b3ff8c4b2831","9047bdb1-92d7-416e-8b98-f686ce4edcdf"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786249191290795002,"uuid":"5f15b4af-9144-4b00-bdf7-e5afc0229841"}